      "textEn": "375\n\nDadau Krishnajinam Bhumirdandam Somo Vanaspatih. Covering the sky, the mother, the sun, the protector of the world. 15. Meaning of the word:\n\nDadau—given, presented; Krishna-ajinam—horn; Bhumih—mother Earth; Dandam—the staff of a celibate; Somah—Moon God; Ne—of; Vanah—husband of the forest; Kaupine—loincloth; Aacharanam—covering the body; Mata—his mother Aditi;\nDyauh—heaven; Chatram—umbrella; Jagat—of the entire universe; Patheh—of the master..\n\nMata Prithvi gave them the deer skin, and Chandradev, the king of plants, gave them the Brahmandand.\n(The stick of a Brahmachari). His mother Aditi gave him clothes for Kaupin and\nThe supreme deity of heaven gave him an umbrella. Kamandalu, the seed of the Vedas, was given by the Saptarshis.\nAkshamala Maharaj Saraswatyavyayatmanah. 16. Meaning of the word\n\nKamandalum—Kamandal, a water vessel; Veda-garbha—Brahmaji; Kushan—Kusha; Sapta-rishayah—The seven sages; Dadu—offered;\nAksha-malaam—A garland of Rudraksha beads; Maharaj—Oh King; Saraswati—Goddess Saraswati; Avyaya-atmanah—To the Lord. Your Highness! Brahmaji gave the Kamandal to Avyay Bhagwan, the Saptarishis gave Kusha and\nMata Saraswati gifted them a Rudraksha garland. Tasmā ityupanitāya yakṣāṭṭapaṭrikāmaṭat. Bhikhya Bhagwati Sakshatdumaadambika Sati. 17. Meaning of the word\n\nTasmai—to them (to Vamanadeva); Iti—in this way; Upanitaaya—whose sacred thread ceremony has been performed; Yaksha-Rat—of the heavens; Koshadhyaksha—chief treasurer; and the king of Yakshas, Kuvera; Patrikam—alms-bowl; Adat—given; Bhiksham—for alms; Bhagavati—Shiva's wife, Mother Bhavani; Sakshat—directly; Uma—Uma; Adat—given; Ambika—the mother of the universe; Sati—a virtuous woman; Sadhvi.\n.\nWhen the Vamana Deva's Yagyopavit Sanskar was completed in this way, Yaksharaja Kuver\ngave them alms in the form of a begging bowl and Shiva's wife, the supreme virtuous woman of the universe, Mother Bhagwati,\ngave them the first alms. By the austerities, by the sacred thread ceremony, and by the assembly, it is possible. Brahmarishiganasanjushtaamatyarochat marishah. 1. Lexicon"
