      "textEn": "377\n\nThen, on the banks of the Narmada, in the north, the Brahmins,\nknown as Bhrigukachchha, were present. The best of the creators, the foremost,\nHaving seen the rising star, as the sun rises. 21. Meaning of the word\n\nTam—to him (Vamanadeva); Narmadayah—of the Narmada river; Tate—on the bank; Uttare—north; Baleh—of the king Bali; Ye—they;\nWho; Ritvijah—the priests engaged in the ritual; Te—they all; Bhrigukachchha-njnke—in the area called Bhrigukachchha; Pravartayantah—proceeding; Bhrigu-vaha—all the Bhrigu dynasty; Kratu-uttamam—an important sacrifice named Ashwamedha; Vyachakshate—saw; Araat—near;\nUditam—rising; Yatha—as; Ravim—to the Sun; On the northern bank of the Narmada River, in an area called Bhrigukachchha, while performing a Yagya (ritual), the Bhriguvanshi Brahmin\nThe priests saw Vamandev as if the sun was rising nearby. Those who are sacrificers, the hosts,\nHaving killed, with the radiance of the Vamana, the king.\nThe sun, having gone to the fort, or the planets,\nSanatkumara, or the creator, with the desire to see. 22. Meaning of the word\n\nThey—all; Ritvijah—priests; Yajamanah— busy in performing the Yagya; Sadasyah— all the members of the assembly; Hat-tvishah— without radiance; Vaman-tejasa— from the radiance of Vamana; Nripah— O King; Suryah— Sun; Kilah— somewhere;\nAayati— is coming; Ut va— or; Vibhavasuha— the fire god; Sanatkumarah— Sanatkumara; Ath— or; Didrikshaya— with the desire to see; Krotah— Yagya.. With the bright radiance of Vamanadeva, Bali Maharaj and all the members of the assembly, including all\npriests became devoid of radiance. They started asking each other if the Sun God himself or Sanatkumar or\nAgni Dev had not come to see the Yagyotsav? Thus, among the disciples, Bhrigu, in many ways,\nArguing, the Lord, Vamana.\nUmbrella, staff, and water pot,\nHe enters the path of the wise. 23). Meaning of the word:\n\nIttham—in this way; s-shishyeshu—with his disciples; bhrigusu—among the bhrigus; anekadha—i