बन गया। अतएव समस्त धर्मों के ज्ञाता बलि महाराज ने शिवजी का अनुसरण करते हुए इस जल",
      "textEn": "379\n\nMeaning of the word\n\nSuch words of welcome; Abhinandya—by welcoming; Ath—in this way; Padau—both lotus feet; Bhagwatam—of the Lord; Baliha—Bali Maharaj; Avanijya—by washing; Archayam Aas—to worship; Mukta-sanga-manoramam—to the liberated souls\nTo the God who looks beautiful. Thus, while properly welcoming the God, who always seems beautiful to the liberated souls,\nBali Maharaj washed his feet and worshiped him. I am the destroyer of the sins of those who are born of impurity.\nI am the auspiciousness that is obtained by the sacrifice of righteousness. Yaddevo Girishchandramaulir\nDadhar Murdhna paraya cha bhaktya. 2. Meaning of the word:\n\nTat-Pad-Shaucham—water obtained by washing the lotus feet of the Lord; Jan-Kalamsha-Apaham—the fruits of all the sins of the people\nWashed away; Sah-Sah-Sah—He (Balarama) did; Dharmavit—Fully known by Dharma; Murdhni—On the head; Adadhat—Holding;\nSu-Mangalam—All auspicious; Yat—That; Dev-Devah—The best among the gods; Girishah—Shiva; Chandra-Maulih—The moon on the forehead\nOne who wears the sign; Dadhar—worn; Murdhna—on the head; Paraya—supreme; Cha—also; Bhaktya—devoutly. The best among the gods, Shiva, who wears the moon on his forehead, the one who wears the water of Ganga coming out of Vishnu's\nthumb, devoutly wears it on his head. Being knowledgeable about religious\nprinciples, Bali Maharaj knew this; as a result, following Shivji,\nhe also placed the water obtained from the cleansing of the lotus feet of God on his\nhead. Meaning: Shiva is called Gangadhara, that is, he who holds the Ganges water on his head. Shiva's forehead is adorned with a crescent moon. Even then, to give utmost respect to God,\nShivji held Ganga water on this symbol. Every single one should follow this example,\nor at least every devotee should do it because Shivji is one of the great men. Similarly,\nBali Maharaj also later became a Mahajan.\nOne Mahajan follows another Mahajan, and\nby following the Mahajan tradition, a person can progress in spiritual consciousness. Ganges water\nis sacred because it comes from the toe of Lord Vishnu's feet. Bali Maharaj\nWashed the lotus feet of Vamandev, and the water with which he washed became equivalent to the Ganges water.\nIt became equal. Therefore, Bali Maharaj, the knower of all religions, following Shiva, this water"
