      "textEn": "35\n\nHaving crossed, with difficulty, Vishnu, the savior, has come. I meditate on the glorious self, remembering that glory. 6. Meaning of the word\n\nYam—Whom; Vinirjitya—Having conquered; Krushchena—With difficulty; Vishnu—In the Varaha incarnation, Lord Vishnu; Kshma-Uddhare—At the time of the salvation of the earth; Aagatam—Appeared before him; Atmanam—Self; Jayinam—Victorious; Mene—Thought; Tat—\nViryam—The valor of Hiranyaksha; Bhuri—Constantly, or more and more; Anusmaran—While contemplating. While redeeming the earth from the ocean of Garbhodaka, Lord Vishnu, in the Varaha incarnation, killed Hiranyaksha, who had appeared before him. Then a fierce battle took place, and God killed him\nwith great difficulty. Later, when God considered Hiranyaksha's extraordinary prowess,\nhe truly felt victorious. Nishamya tadvadham bhrata Hiranyakashipu: pura.\nHantum bhratrahnam krodho jagam nilayam hareh. 7. Meaning of the word\nNishamya—Hearing; Tat-vadham—the killing of Hiranyakashipu; Bhrata—brother; Hiranyakashipu—Hiranyakashipu; Puraa—long ago;\nHantum—to kill; Bhrata-hannam—the murderer of one's own brother; Krodhah—extremely angry; Jagam—went; Nilayam—abode;\nHareh—of the Lord..\nWhen Hiranyakashipu heard that his brother had been killed, he became extremely angry.\nBeing very angry, he went to his abode to kill Vishnu, the murderer of his brother. Having seen the demon, with a trident in hand, like a destroyer. Chintayamas Kalagno Vishnurmaaya Vinaam Varahah. Meaning of the word.\n\nTam—to him (Hiranyakashipu); Ayantham—coming forward; Samalokyam— looking closely; Shul-panim— with one's hand in his hand; Krutant-vat— like the direct time; Chintayam-as— thought; Kal-gyahan— knowing the movement of time;\nVishnu—Vishnu; Mayavinam— of all kinds of illusionists; Varaham— chief, head.\n.\n\nSeeing Hiranyakashipu moving forward with a trident in his hand, like the direct form of time, all the\nthe best among the illusionists and Lord Vishnu, who knows 