ittle; Vrṇe—Among; I am asking; Aham—I; Varad-rishabhāt—From the best of the best-giving sages; Padāṇi—Feet; Trayin—Three; Daitya-indra—Oh, king of demons; Sammitāni—Equal to measure; Pada—By foot; Mama—Mine.\nOh, you demon king! Such a noble and generous donor, I, measuring with my own feet, only\nask for three paces of land. Meaning: Lord Vamana, by measuring with his feet, only wanted three paces of land. They did not need more land than was absolutely necessary. But although he had disguised himself as a normal human child, in reality, he wanted to donate the land surrounded by the upper, middle, and lower worlds."
